Here's a simple MATLAB code that identifies the tense used in a given sentence. This code uses regular expressions to match different tense patterns. You can add more patterns as needed.

```matlab
function tense = identify_tense(sentence)
    % Regular expressions for different tenses
    present_simple = '^(\w+)\b(?:is|are|am)\b';
    past_simple = '^(\w+)\b(?:was|were)\b';
    future_simple = '^(\w+)\b(?:will|shall)\b';
    present_continuous = '^(\w+)\b(?:is|are|am)\b(?:ing)$';
    past_continuous = '^(\w+)\b(?:was|were)\b(?:ing)$';
    future_continuous = '^(\w+)\b(?:will|shall)\b(?:ing)$';
    present_perfect = '^(\w+)\b(?:has|have|had)\b(?:been)$';
    past_perfect = '^(\w+)\b(?:had)\b(?:been)$';
    future_perfect = '^(\w+)\b(?:will|shall)\b(?:have)\b(?:been)$';

    % Match the tense pattern in the sentence
    match = regexp(sentence, [present_simple, past_simple, future_simple, present_continuous, past_continuous, future_continuous, present_perfect, past_perfect, future_perfect], 'match');

    % Extract the matched tense pattern
    tense = strsplit(match{1}, ' ')[2];
end

% Test the function with the given example sentence
sentence = 'I would like to have a meeting today';
tense = identify_tense(sentence);
disp(['The tense used in the sentence is: ', tense]);
```

